      <div type="clause" n="28.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 28.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="512–513" ed="#liebermann"/>E si li guardireve averad XXX hides, quite serrad pur sun travail.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="512–513" ed="#liebermann"/>Et wardireve si avrad XXX hides quites<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_28-1.lnote.oe.a"/> pur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#LeisWl_28-1.lnote.oe.9"/> son travail<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#LeisWl_28-1.lnote.oe.10"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="512–513" ed="#liebermann"/>Et gwardereve, id est prepositus custodum, habebit XXX hidas quietas pro labore suo.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="28.1" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="266" ed="#robertson"/>E si li guardireve averad XXX hides, quite serrad pur sun travail.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="512–513" ed="#liebermann"/>28, 1. Jedoch der Wachinspector<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_28-1.lnote.de.1"/>, [sogar<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_28-1.lnote.de1.a"/>] wenn er 30 Hufen besitzt, soll wegen seiner Amtsmühe frei sein<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_28-1.lnote.de1.b"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">28, 1. But the inspector of the watch, [even] if he possesses 30 hides, shall be free on account of the trouble of his office.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="267" ed="#robertson"/>And even if the Commander of the Watch has 30 hides, his duty shall grant him exemption in this matter.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="513"><ref target="clause:Rect_18-to-18-1">Rect 18</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">*vgl. Rect. 18</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 266–267 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 512–513, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_28-1.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">512</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vorlage von IL versteht nicht, dass</hi> 30 Hiden <hi rend="italic">einen für einen Bauern unmöglich grossen Besitz bedeutet: der</hi> wardireve <hi rend="italic">bleibt frei, so reich er auch sei</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The exemplar of IL does not understand that 30 hides means a holding impossibly large for a peasant: the wardireve remains exempt, however rich he may be</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_28-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">512</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">per <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">per Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_28-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">512</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">travaile <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">travaile <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_28-1.lnote.oe.a-2" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">512</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">29—32 <hi rend="italic">gehören inhaltlich zusammen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">29—32 belong together in content</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_28-1.lnote.de1.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">513</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">soll 30 H. w. s. A. frei haben <hi rend="italic">IL</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">shall have 30 hides free on account of his labour IL</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_28-1.lnote.de1.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">513</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">von jener Wächterstellung</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">from that post of watchman</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_28-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">290</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">weardgerefa</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi>; sonst nicht nachweisbar) birgt wohl wie <hi rend="italic">weardman</hi> im ersten Glied das fm. <hi rend="italic">weard</hi>. Mit Unrecht versteht Kelham <hi rend="italic">wardreeve</hi> ‘Vogt eines Stadtviertels’; letztere Bed. ist erst seit Ende 12. Jhs. belegt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">weardgerefa</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi>; not otherwise attested) probably contains, like <hi rend="italic">weardman</hi>, the fem. <hi rend="italic">weard</hi> in its first element. Kelham wrongly understands <hi rend="italic">wardreeve</hi> as ‘reeve of a ward of a town’; the latter meaning is attested only from the end of the 12th cent.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
